 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 677123,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "An online automotive magazine is running a social media campaign to increase paid subscriptions. Which of the following would be an example of a conversion on its website given the campaign’s goal?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1345743,
     "content_html": "A visitor uses the search tool on the website to search “vintage European cars.”",
     "correctness": "0.0",
     "feedback_html": "That&#8217;s not correct. The definition of a conversion depends on the goal of the campaign. If the goal of the campaign were to increase usage of the search tool, it would make sense that this answer would be a conversion. Because the goal of the campaign is to increase paid subscriptions, a visitor who enters their payment information and contact information and clicks &#8220;place order&#8221; would be a conversion."
    },
    {
     "id": 1345742,
     "content_html": "A visitor enters their email address to receive updates.",
     "correctness": "0.0",
     "feedback_html": "That&#8217;s not correct. The definition of a conversion depends on the goal of the campaign. If the goal of the campaign were to collect email addresses from visitors, it would make sense that this answer would be a conversion. Because the goal of the campaign is to increase paid subscriptions, a visitor who enters their payment information and contact information and clicks &#8220;place order&#8221; would be a conversion."
    },
    {
     "id": 1345744,
     "content_html": "A visitor enters their payment information and contact information and clicks on “place order.”",
     "correctness": "1.0",
     "feedback_html": "Because the goal of the campaign is to increase paid subscriptions, a visitor who enters their payment information and contact information and clicks &#8220;place order&#8221; would be a conversion."
    },
    {
     "id": 1345741,
     "content_html": "A visitor downloads the app on their mobile phone.",
     "correctness": "0.0",
     "feedback_html": "That&#8217;s not correct. The definition of a conversion depends on the goal of the campaign. If the goal of the campaign were to increase the number of apps downloaded, it would make sense that this answer would be a conversion. Because the goal of the campaign is to increase paid subscriptions, a visitor who enters their payment information and contact information and clicks &#8220;place order&#8221; would be a conversion."
    }
   ],
